{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542129-clan-lasombra-trilogy","id":1542129,"title":"Clan Lasombra Trilogy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-14T13:37:21-07:00","id":1542129,"title":"Clan Lasombra Trilogy","content":"BOOK 1<br /> SHARDS<br /> <br /> <i><img width=\"250\" height=\"423\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/LasombraTril2.webp?w=250&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/LasombraTril2.webp?w=250&amp;ssl=1\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i0.wp.com/beforewegoblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/LasombraTril2.webp?w=250&amp;ssl=1\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> \u201cThese hands have spilled more blood than I can imagine in one place. These eyes have looked on countless sins. These teeth have drained the gift of life again and again. I told myself for a thousand years that I was all the things my sire wasn\u2019t. But I was just like him: I have preyed on others for my own ends. God won\u2019t take the curse away, but I must atone as I can. It\u2019s baptism, if you want to call that. I\u2019m going to let fire strip off what water can\u2019t.\u201d</i> \u2013 Lucita de Aragorn, <i>Shards</i><br /> <br /> Female antiheroes are still fairly rare in fantasy novel. This is certainly not something that is absolute, don\u2019t get me wrong. One of my favorite characters growing up was Kitiara Uth Matar who was almost as much a protagonist in the Dragonlance Legends books books as Raistlin Majere. My wife and I met on the Anita Blake forums with the titular character having been designed to be a hard boiled detective who was willing to kill anyone she had to in order to keep the fragile peace of Saint Louis. Then there\u2019s Lucita de Aragon, a character that only had a few appearances in White Wolf\u2019s World of Darkness novels yet remains one of the singularly most memorable characters they ever created.<br /> <br /> Lucita is an eight hundred year old vampire, one of the oldest most active undead around, who was a literal princess when alive. However, she was a rebellious young woman who her father assigned to the church to discipline. Unfortunately, like today, the institution was not always full of good individuals and she fell prey to a predator. This being the World of Darkness, said predator was a vampire named Father Luis Moncada who turned her into one of the undead. From there, Lucita spent centuries opposing her sire while sustaining her luxurious lifestyle as a highly paid assassin of her own kind. That is, until, <a href=\"https://beforewegoblog.com/review-clan-novel-lasombra-by-richard-dansky/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Clan Novel: Lasombra</i></a> when she finally killed Moncada with the help of her lover, Fatima al-Faqadi.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, victory has robbed Lucita of one of the things that she used to define herself as an undead survivor. Moncada was one of the Sabbat, a monstrous religious fanatic, and as close to absolute evil as you could get. By opposing him, Lucita could always keep away the Beast by saying, \u201cI\u2019m not as bad as that guy.\u201d With Moncada dead, Lucita is left with the uncomfortable realization she\u2019s now only able to define herself by her own sins and they\u2019re horrifying. She\u2019s not a friendly neighborhood vampire or a hero nor is she likely to become one. However, she needs to figure out something to define herself as when there\u2019s no one left to defend herself against.<br /> <br /> Lucita is a fantastic character and this book allows a lot more insight into her than the original Clan Novel starring her (albeit not quite as much as the Dark Ages Clan Novel by David Niall Wilson). A lot of insight is had in the fact that she wants to atone and be a better person but, really, just isn\u2019t sorry or regretful for any of the evil deeds she\u2019s done. Not really. It\u2019s a nice change of pace of vampire fiction and the fact our heroine is struggling with the fact, \u201cYeah, I\u2019m genuinely evil and that sucks\u201d is an interesting character journey.<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, for a book written by a dude in the early 2000s, Lucita\u2019s bisexuality isn\u2019t written for titillation. Her connection with Fatima is something that is depicted as motivated by deep loneliness and a genuine emotional connection between two deadly killers. Unfortunately, Fatima really does believe God has her back and has never lost her sense of purpose. Fatima is deeply-deluded about undead being something more than monsters but at least that is an ethos. If forced to choose between her clan and Lucita, she might choose Lucita but she\u2019s never going to choose Lucita over God. Lucita just flat out does not share Fatima\u2019s faith even though said faith among undead doesn\u2019t preclude a relationship between two women. Sadly, Lucita\u2019s other lost love, Anatole, isn\u2019t there to mediate.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, the Clan Lasombra Trilogy is one of the best series produced for the Old World of Darkness fiction line and this is a great introduction to it. It\u2019s also a good book to purchase for Pride month. You\u2019d probably have to read <i>Clan Novel: Lasombra</i> to get as much out of it as you should, though. It\u2019s enough for me to wish they\u2019d make a new set of books starring Lucita, though. Bruce Baugh\u2019s version of Lucita is far more erudite, thoughtful, and tragic than Richard Dansky even if she\u2019s far less sympathetic than David Niall Wilson\u2019s.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T13:38:04-07:00","id":1542130,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm re-reading the series that derrailed Lucita.<br /> <br /> For better or worse.<br /> <br /> (Worse)<br /> <br /> Feel free to pipe in folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T13:58:25-07:00","id":1542131,"title":"","content":"It was a good read that reinforced the tradegy that vampires get more monstrous with age and they need stuff to cleave to stay &quot;sane&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T14:23:10-07:00","id":1542133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542129-clan-lasombra-trilogy?p=1542130#post1542130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm re-reading the series that derrailed Lucita.<br /> <br /> For better or worse.<br /> <br /> (Worse)<br /> <br /> Feel free to pipe in folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm actually very interested in what Lucita's character is, so I'm mostly here to read/learn. I've been depicting her in Transylvania Chronicles as a somewhat remorseful and skeptical knightess errant, who initially can't fight the submission under Mon\u00e7ada, but once the terrible crimes of the Clan of Shadow come to bear in the Anarch War, she finally takes her own way. Which leads her to become an Anarch, despite all things that would push her away from it, like being in a Clan mostly viewed by the Camarilla as criminal (and the former viewing the Montano-bound Lasombra as weak and subservient), and her sire being one of the top Lasombra active. <br /> <br /> So I'm quite eager to hear about it.<br /> The only novel I do plan to read though, is the Dark Ages Saga. I first read the Tzimisce one (trying to understand what the hell happened to Illias, Vykos and Dracon), and then the Ventrue, and good god what good writing and drama it has!! Then I started reading the first of the saga, Nosferatu, very good too. After trudging a bit through the Haquimite one... I skipped it, the plot and characters alienated me. But I'm yet to continue to read it. And I want to see how Anatole and Lucita are depicted in the saga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T14:24:33-07:00","id":1542134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542129-clan-lasombra-trilogy?p=1542131#post1542131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a good read that reinforced the tradegy that vampires get more monstrous with age and they need stuff to cleave to stay &quot;sane&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect this may be why Dark Ages Lucita might come across as more sympathetic than Final Nights Lucita. <br /> <br /> There is a short story Bruce Baugh did for the Clan Anthology in which Lucita encounters Mozart in Vienna, which probably works better if the reader is familiar with Mozart's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T15:03:41-07:00","id":1542136,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the larger thing is that Path of Night Lucita is far less interesting than Path of Humanity (however low) Lucita.<br /> <br /> It was in GEHENNA, that Beckett and Anatole basically say that Lucita is just like a shallow parody of herself.<br /> <br /> Which was fascinating because that hits far harder than decrying her being &quot;evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, Lucita takes it like a Toreador being called &quot;ya, basic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T15:12:34-07:00","id":1542139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542129-clan-lasombra-trilogy?p=1542134#post1542134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect this may be why Dark Ages Lucita might come across as more sympathetic than Final Nights Lucita.<br /> <br /> There is a short story Bruce Baugh did for the Clan Anthology in which Lucita encounters Mozart in Vienna, which probably works better if the reader is familiar with Mozart's work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense that Dark Ages Lucita is more likeable then her modern nights self. Her days as a living breathing humans female isn't quite the faded memory that it would be for Moncada or definitely her grandsire De Ruiz who was already a respected elder in Iberia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}